 simplex virus infections</article-title><source>Med Microbiol Immunol</source><year>2007</year><volume>196</volume><fpage>89</fpage><lpage>94</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17165093</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00430-006-0031-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>ZA</given-names></name><name><surname>Wald</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Morrow</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Selke</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Zeh</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Corey</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of serologic status and cesarean delivery on transmission rates of herpes simplex virus from mother to infant</article-title><source>JAMA</source><year>2003</year><volume>289</volume><fpage>203</fpage><lpage>209</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12517231</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/jama.289.2.203</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Desselberger</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Herpes simplex virus infection in pregnancy: diagnosis and significance</article-title><source>Intervirology</source><year>1998</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>185</fpage><lpage>190</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10213894</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1159/000024934</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Weiss</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Epidemiology of herpes simplex virus type 2 infection in the developing world</article-title><source>Herpes</source><year>2004</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>24A</fpage><lpage>35A</lpage><pub-id pub